=== Prompt ===
Tell me about Donald Trump.

=== Normal Response ===
Donald John Trump is born on June 14, 1946, in Queens, New York City. He is an American businessman, real estate developer, and politician who served as the 45th President of the United States from January 20, 2017, to January 20, 2021.

Trump was born into a wealthy family and has been involved in various business ventures throughout his career. He is best known for his role in the development of luxury real estate, particularly in the New York City area. He also gained significant media attention through his reality television show "The Apprentice," which he hosted from 2004 to 2016.

In 2016, Trump ran for president as a candidate of the Republican Party. He won the election and became the first U.S. president to not have previously held public office or military service. During his presidency, Trump implemented several policies and initiatives, including tax reform, border security measures, and changes to immigration laws. He also faced numerous controversies and legal challenges during his time in office.

After leaving office, Trump continued to be a prominent figure in American politics and media. He has since founded a new political party, the "Don't Run" Party, and remains active in various business and political activities.

